{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide"},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"EntityStore"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a dictionary with insertion-order iteration. Entities must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":" as the ID type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var cards = EntityStore<Card>()","","cards[card.id] = card                      \/\/ Insert or update — recorded","cards.modify(card.id) { $0.title = \"New\" } \/\/ In-place — recorded only if value changes","cards[card.id] = nil                       \/\/ Delete — recorded","","let card = cards[cardID]                   \/\/ O(1) lookup","let all  = cards.values                    \/\/ Insertion-ordered array","","cards.sort { $0.sortIndex < $1.sortIndex } \/\/ Only marks moved entities","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }          \/\/ Rebuilds index in one pass"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every mutation is tracked in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that the middleware drains after each reducer call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Bulk Deletion","anchor":"Bulk-Deletion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifts the storage array’s tail and reindexes the shifted entries — O(tail) per delete, so a loop of k subscript deletes costs O(n·k). To delete many entities at once, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(ids:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (when you have the IDs) or ","type":"text"},{"code":"removeAll(where:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (when you have a predicate) instead: both remove everything in a single pass with one index rebuild, record the same deletions, and cancel pending upserts exactly like the subscript.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["cards.remove(ids: selection)          \/\/ One pass, not a subscript loop","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Merging (Re-hydration)","anchor":"Merging-Re-hydration","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Replacing an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" after startup destroys any in-memory state that was loaded lazily after initial hydration. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — entities only in the other store are always added, and the closure decides whether an incoming value overwrites the current one:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Absorb DB rows; take an incoming row only when the current one","\/\/ lacks lazily-computed data.","campaigns.merge(from: EntityStore(allFromDB)) { current, incoming in","    current.calculationState == nil && incoming.calculationState != nil","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge"},{"text":" does not record changes — it has hydration semantics like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"reconcile vs merge","type":"heading","anchor":"reconcile-vs-merge"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two answer different questions:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Stance","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep everything, absorb what’s new"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is authoritative "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"except"}]},{"type":"text","text":" where you say otherwise"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removes rows","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Never"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removingMissing"},{"type":"text","text":" and the ID isn’t preserved"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Conflicts","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your closure decides, per pair","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage wins unless the ID is preserved"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile"},{"text":" is what lets a remote edit or a remote deletion surface mid-session rather than waiting for the next launch. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"text":" is the caller’s list of IDs that carry unflushed local intent; the store’s own un-drained ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"text":" are folded in automatically, so a pending local deletion is never resurrected even when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"text":" is empty.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["cards.reconcile(with: EntityStore(rowsFromDisk), preserving: dirtyIDs, removingMissing: true)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"code":"merge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", it records no changes — every value it writes or removes already reflects what is in storage, so recording them would echo each remote change straight back as a local write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most apps never call this directly; ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator.rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does, and computes ","type":"text"},{"code":"preserving","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for you.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"restore(from:)","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"restorefrom"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" replaces all entities with those from the source store while recording the diff as changes for persistence. Used by undo\/redo (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deletions","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs in self but absent from source"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Upserts"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — IDs that are new or whose values differ","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Unchanged","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — identical values produce no change records"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Remote-deletions-are-not-undoable","text":"Remote deletions are not undoable","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One class of ID is skipped: anything "},{"code":"reconcile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" removed because storage no longer held it. Those IDs are kept in "},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" will neither re-add them nor record a change for them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without that, undo resurrects rows other devices deleted. An undo snapshot taken before the deletion still contains the entity, so restoring it records an ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"upsert","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — which flushes as a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"creation","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed the row was gone. Undo is scoped to what the local user did; a deletion made on another device isn’t that.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ID leaves the set as soon as it becomes local again — an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store[id] = entity"},{"type":"text","text":", or storage handing the row back on a later merge — so a row that another device deletes and then restores is undoable once more. The set survives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resetChanges()"},{"type":"text","text":", because a flush ends a pending write’s life, not a deletion’s."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ \"3 items were deleted on another device.\"","cards.remotelyRemovedIDs.count"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stores that never sync never populate it, and "},{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes exactly the path it did before."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswit